    "problem_statement": "SVG image generation returns None instead of SVG element\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen generating QR codes using the SVG image factory, the `_svg` method returns `None` instead of the expected SVG element, causing failures when trying to save or use the generated image.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nimport qrcode\nfrom qrcode.image import svg\nimport io\n\nqr = qrcode.QRCode()\nqr.add_data('test data')\nimg = qr.make_image(image_factory=svg.SvgImage)\nimg.save(io.BytesIO())  # This will fail\n```\n\nThe above code raises an `AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no attribute 'write'` because the SVG generation is returning `None` instead of a proper SVG element.\n\nThis also affects command line usage:\n\n```bash\nqr 'test data' --factory svg\n```"
  }
